  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d3d793df-3e96-4f6d-8b4a-653354f7b9e5.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 179px;\"/></p><p>Direction of magnetic field is in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Force acting on wire is given by, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>l</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>×</mo><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>As, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>B</mi><mo> </mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p>",
